      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The majority will hold that 8 U.S.C. \u00a7 1188(g)(2) authorizes the Department of Labor to impose and seek remedies but does not clearly authorize the agency to conclusively adjudicate contested monetary liability in-house, so the Third Circuit's judgment is affirmed without deciding the Article III question."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The majority's rule will be narrow: it will cover DOL's in-house adjudication of H-2A penalties and back wages under \u00a7 1188(g)(2), preserve DOL's ability to administer certifications and pursue remedies in an Article III court, and leave other statutory agency-adjudication schemes unresolved."
    }
  ],
